Registers `a` and `b` start at a = 1, b = 2. After one rising clock edge, what do they hold?

```verilog
always @(posedge clk) begin
  // Run statements in source order.
  a = b;
  b = a;
end
```

A designer writes this to describe a simple mux-like block. What does synthesis build for `y`?

```verilog
// Each branch chooses a data input.
always @(*)
  if (sel == 2'b00)      y = a;
  else if (sel == 2'b01) y = b;
  else if (sel == 2'b10) y = c;
```
